---
/** The Kit. Every fact on this page comes from the CAD notes (~/workspace/SLDP CAD on the build
    machine) or from the team poster (docs/README.md, Theme). Do not add a spec, a count or a
    price that is not in one of those. The models are exported by scripts/step_to_glb.py:
    when the CAD version changes, re-export and change the captions and the Status row.
    Since 2026-11-23 the page shows Final v3, and its numbers are from the READMEs of
    Final v1 and Final v3 in the CAD folder. The prices under "What it costs" are the team's
    cost table of 2026-11-24 (docs/cost-table-2026-11-24.png), kept in src/data/compare.ts.
    Since 2026-11-25 the page is five sections and a closing band. What a classroom needs
    besides the parts is on For teachers, and how a lesson runs is on Lessons: this page
    links to both and repeats neither. The circuit and the specifications are one row that
    opens, for whoever will build the hand. */
import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ModelViewer from '../components/ModelViewer.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/SectionLabel.astro';
import CircuitDiagram from '../components/CircuitDiagram.astro';
import { p, KIT_REQUEST } from '../lib/url';
import { cost, costTotals, money } from '../data/compare';
import { printed, bought, CLASS_SIZE, GROUP } from '../data/kit';

const specs = [
  { k: 'Controller', v: 'Arduino Mega 2560' },
  { k: 'Fingers', v: 'Four finger modules and a thumb' },
  { k: 'Motors', v: 'Six DC motors: one in each finger, two in the thumb' },
  { k: 'Finger drive', v: 'The motor turns a threaded rod, which pulls the finger closed' },
  { k: 'Finger curl', v: 'Straight to 72°' },
  { k: 'Finger module', v: '33 mm wide, 291 mm long (about 1.3 × 11.5 in)' },
  { k: 'Printed parts', v: 'PLA plastic on an ordinary 3D printer, with no support material' },
  { k: 'Size', v: 'About 32 × 26 × 11 cm (12.6 × 10.2 × 4.3 in), lying flat with the thumb out to the side' },
  { k: 'Ages', v: '11 and up' },
];

const bill = costTotals();
const classHands = CLASS_SIZE / GROUP;
---
<Base title="The Kit" description="The HelpingHand kit: a modular robotic hand that students design, wire, and program themselves.">
  <PageHeader
    title="A robotic hand students build themselves."
    lede="HelpingHand is a modular robotic hand that students design, wire, and program themselves. They learn mechanics, circuits, and coding one lesson at a time, not by following a manual."
  >
    {/* The page's one status line. The captions and the tables below say nothing more about it. */}
    <p class="meta mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
      <span class="badge">Prototype</span>
      <span>This is the team's current design. The first full hand is not printed yet.</span>
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>The hand</SectionLabel>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="statement">Four fingers, a thumb, and everything that drives them.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-5">Each finger is its own module with its own motor. The modules sit side by side in the palm, the thumb slides on beside them, and the electronics sit under one curved shell that is the back of the hand.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-4 text-rule">The grey parts are the screws and nuts. The motors and the boards are inside, out of sight.</p>
      </div>
      <ModelViewer
        src="/models/hand-final-v3.glb"
        alt="3D model of the HelpingHand: four fingers and a thumb on a palm, with the electronics under a curved shell on the back"
        label="The whole hand"
        height="h-[22rem] md:h-[30rem]"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>One finger</SectionLabel>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="statement">One motor curls three segments.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-5">The motor turns a threaded rod. A block rides along the rod and pulls a link, and the links carry that one motion through all three segments of the finger, from straight to a 72° curl.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-4">It is the unit of the whole curriculum: small enough to understand completely, real enough to be worth programming.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary mt-7" href={p('/lessons/beginner/01-finger-module/')}>Open Lesson 1</a>
      </div>
      <ModelViewer
        src="/models/finger-final-v3.glb"
        alt="3D model of one finger module: a three-segment finger on a long motor housing"
        label="One finger module"
        height="h-80 md:h-[24rem]"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="cost">
    <SectionLabel>What it costs</SectionLabel>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="statement">{money(bill.total)} in parts for one hand.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-5">That is every part the team has priced, the plastic for the printed parts, and a fifth on top for what is not listed yet. One hand is shared by a group of {GROUP} students, so a class of {CLASS_SIZE} needs {classHands} hands: <strong>{money(bill.total * classHands)}</strong>.</p>
        <p class="measure mt-4 text-rule">It is the cost of the parts of the current prototype, not a selling price.</p>
        <p class="mt-4"><a class="link" href={p('/problem/#compare')}>See it beside five other kits</a></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="result-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">How many</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">Each</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">Cost</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {cost.rows.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{r.item}</th>
                  <td class="text-right!">{r.qty}</td>
                  <td class="text-right!">{money(r.unit)}</td>
                  <td class="text-right!">{money(r.qty * r.unit)}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Contingency ({cost.contingency * 100}%)</th>
                <td></td><td></td>
                <td class="text-right!">{money(bill.extra)}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="font-bold!">Total</th>
                <td class="result"></td><td class="result"></td>
                <td class="result text-right! font-bold">{money(bill.total)}</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta measure mt-3">The team's cost table of {cost.date}. Unit prices are from the <a class="link" href={cost.src.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{cost.src.label}</a>. Screws, wiring and the two push buttons fall under the contingency.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="parts">
    <SectionLabel>What is in the box</SectionLabel>
    <p class="statement">Every part of one hand is either printed or bought.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lead">Printed</h3>
        <ul class="rows mt-4">
          {printed.map((b) => (
            <li><p>{b.item}</p><p>{b.note}</p></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lead">Bought</h3>
        <ul class="rows mt-4">
          {bought.map((b) => (
            <li><p>{b.item}{b.qty > 1 && <span class="ml-2 font-normal tabular-nums text-rule">×{b.qty}</span>}</p><p>{b.note}</p></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="measure mt-8">Besides the parts, a classroom needs a 3D printer, a computer and small hex keys. <a class="link" href={p('/teachers/#need')}>What you need</a> is on For teachers.</p>
  </section>

  {/* The circuit is the one on the team's final prototype poster (24 Nov 2026), redrawn in
      CircuitDiagram.astro. It and the specifications are for whoever will build the hand, so
      they open on request: a link to #circuit opens the row (the script below). */}
  <section class="section">
    <details class="more" id="circuit">
      <summary><span class="more-title">Circuit and specifications</span><span class="meta">The wiring drawing and the numbers, for whoever builds the hand.</span></summary>
      <div class="split">
        <p class="statement">Six motors on one Arduino.</p>
        <p class="measure">One Arduino Mega 2560 controls two motor shields, and each shield drives three DC motors. A tilt sensor shares the same connection, and two push buttons give control by hand. The motors run from their own 7.2 V battery. A Wi-Fi module is proposed and not built yet.</p>
      </div>
      <CircuitDiagram class="mt-8" />
      <div class="split mt-14">
        <div>
          <p class="statement">Printed parts, an Arduino, and ordinary screws.</p>
          <p class="measure mt-5">When a part breaks, print another. When a student wants a different finger, design one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="result-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Spec</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {specs.map((s) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row" class="whitespace-nowrap">{s.k}</th>
                  <td>{s.v}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <script>
    // A link to #circuit lands on a closed row: open it.
    const openTarget = () => {
      const el = location.hash ? document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1)) : null;
      if (el instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) el.open = true;
    };
    openTarget();
    addEventListener('hashchange', openTarget);
  </script>

  <section class="band band-close">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionLabel>Request a kit</SectionLabel>
      <div class="split">
        <p class="statement text-white">Kits are not for sale yet. Tell us about your class.</p>
        <div>
          <p class="measure text-(--on-navy-soft)">“Request a kit” starts an email to all four of us, with the three things we need to know already asked: your school, the grade and the class size.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary mt-6" href={KIT_REQUEST}>Request a kit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
